Hi,

I've noticed a bug in gl.map.interactive. I'm using the dev version of dartR (2.3.3) on windows, and I don't remember this being an issue before I switched to the dev version. Basically, when there is only one population, the map produced by gl.map.interactive is zoomed out to show the whole world, and the population label appears up the top outside the map. I've attached an example of what this looks like. There is no issue when multiple pops are specified.

Rhiannon

